      "description": "330-PS-8455 (USN 709907):  “Admiral Drops In”   One way to get on board a submarine is demonstrated by Rear Admiral Elton W. Grenfell, Commander, Submarine Force Pacific Fleet, as he descends on the nuclear submarine USS Nautilus (SSN 571), at sea off the West Coast.   Admiral Grenfell visited Nautilus while it was engaged in training exercises with the fleet.  He flew in from USS Princeton (CV 37), in background, via helicopter June 12.   He rode on board to Seattle, Washington, and disembarked upon her arrival there June 15.   Photograph released June 25, 1957.  (12/30/2014).",
